Commit Transaction');
INSERT INTO "step_examples" ("id", "script_step_id", "locale", "position", "title", "description", "body") VALUES (423, 17, 'en', 3, 'Example 4', 'The main script opens a transaction, sets TextField, then calls a sub-script. Because the sub-script is called while a transaction is already open, its Open Transaction step is skipped, TextField is set to a different value, then the condition in the Revert Transaction step is evaluated.

If NumberField is 1, the current transaction (opened in the main script) is reverted. The sub-script''s Commit Transaction step is skipped, then control passes back to the main script''s Commit Transaction step, skipping any steps after Perform Script. When the main script is finished, the value of TextField is unchanged.

If NumberField is 0, then the sub-script doesn''t revert the transaction, so control passes back to the step after Perform Script, where TextField is set to abc123 and the transaction is committed.

Main script', 'Open Transaction [ ]
 Set Field [ Table::TextField ; "abc" ]
 Perform Script [ Specified: From list ; "Sub-script" ; Parameter: ]
 Set Field [ Table::TextField ; "abc123" ]
Commit Transaction
Open Transaction [ ]
 Set Field [ Table::TextField ; "xyz456" ]
 Revert Transaction [ Condition: Table::NumberField = 1 ]
Commit Transaction');
INSERT INTO "step_examples" ("id", "script_step_id", "locale", "position", "title", "description", "body") VALUES (424, 18, 'en', 0, 'Example 1', 'Goes to the Print Invoices layout and pauses. The user can click a Continue button on the status toolbar or the layout to print the records.', 'Go to Layout ["Print Invoices"]
Pause/Resume Script [Indefinitely]
Print [Restore: Printer; With dialog: Off]
Go to Layout [original layout]');
INSERT INTO "step_examples" ("id", "script_step_id", "locale", "position", "title", "description", "body") VALUES (425, 19, 'en', 0, 'Example 1', 'Runs the "Print Invoice Report" script with no parameters.', 'Go to Layout ["Invoice Report"]
Perform Script [Specified: From list; "Print Invoice Report"; Parameter: ]');
INSERT INTO "step_examples" ("id", "script_step_id", "locale", "position", "title", "description", "body") VALUES (426, 19, 'en', 1, 'Example 2', 'Uses a field value, Customer Name, as the parameter. Invoices for the current customer are returned in a new window with the Invoice Report layout.

Main script: Current Customer Invoices', 'Find Matching Records [Replace; Invoices::Customer ID]
#Calls the "View Customer Invoices" sub-script defined below
Perform Script [Specified: From list; "View Customer Invoices"; Parameter: Invoices::Customer Name]
New Window [Style: Document; Name: "Customer: " & Get ( ScriptParameter ); Using layout: "Invoice Report" (Invoices)]
Sort Records [Restore; With dialog: Off]');
INSERT INTO "step_examples" ("id", "script_step_id", "locale", "position", "title", "description", "body") VALUES (427, 19, 'en', 2, 'Example 3', 'Shows a custom dialog box with the default button and button 2, then performs the script named "Button1" or "Button2" depending on the user''s choice returned in Get ( LastMessageChoice ).', 'Show Custom Dialog [ "Do you want to continue?" ]
Perform Script [ Specified: By name ; "Button" & Get ( LastMessageChoice ) ; Parameter: ]');
INSERT INTO "step_examples" ("id", "script_step_id", "locale", "position", "title", "description", "body") VALUES (428, 20, 'en', 0, 'Example 1', 'Runs a script on the server and sends the current layout name, customer ID, and customer email address as the script parameter. The server navigates to the layout and record specified in the parameter, saves a snapshot link of the current record, emails the snapshot link to the email address specified in the parameter, and returns a result. The client fetches the script result from the server and displays it in a custom dialog box.

Main script: Email snapshot link (Client)', 'Perform Script on Server [Specified: From list ; "Email snapshot link (Server)" ; Parameter: List ( Get ( LayoutName ) ; Customers::ID ; Customers::Email ) ; Wait for completion: On]
Show Custom Dialog [Get ( ScriptResult )]
Go to Layout [GetValue ( Get ( ScriptParameter ) ; 1 )]
Enter Find Mode [Pause: Off]
Set Field [Customers::ID; GetValue ( Get ( ScriptParameter ) ; 2 )]
Perform Find [ ]
Set Variable [$PATH; Value:Get ( TemporaryPath ) & "Snapshot.fmpsl"]
Save Records as Snapshot Link ["$PATH"; Current record ; Create folders: Off]
Send Mail [Send via SMTP Server; With dialog: Off; To: GetValue ( Get ( ScriptParameter ) ; 3 ); "$PATH"]
Exit Script [Text Result: "Snapshot link sent."]');
INSERT INTO "step_examples" ("id", "script_step_id", "locale", "position", "title", "description", "body") VALUES (429, 21, 'en', 0, 'Example 1', 'Runs a script on the server and sends the current layout name, customer ID, and customer email address as the script parameter. The server navigates to the layout and record specified in the parameter, saves a snapshot link of the current record, emails the snapshot link to the email address specified in the parameter, and returns a result. The client fetches the script result from the server and displays it in a custom dialog box. To use the server script''s result in the callback script, note that the callback script itself uses Get(ScriptResult), which returns the value passed by the server script''s Exit Script script step.

Main script: Email snapshot link (Client)', 'Perform Script on Server with Callback [ Specified: From list ; "Email snapshot link (Server)" ;
Parameter: List ( Get ( LayoutName ) ; Customers::ID ; Customers::Email ) ;
Callback script specified: From list ; "Complete message (Client)" ; Parameter: ; State: Continue ]
Go to Layout [ GetValue ( Get ( ScriptParameter ) ; 1 ) ; Animation: None ]
Enter Find Mode [ Pause: Off ]
Set Field [ Customers::ID ; GetValue ( Get ( ScriptParameter ) ; 2 ) ]
Perform Find [ ]
Set Variable [ $PATH ; Value: Get ( TemporaryPath ) & "Snapshot.fmpsl" ]
Save Records as Snapshot Link [ "$PATH" ; Current record ; Create folders: Off ]
Send Mail [ Send via SMTP Server ; No dialog ; To: GetValue ( Get ( ScriptParameter ) ; 3 ) ; "$PATH" ]
Exit Script [ Text Result: "Snapshot link sent." ]
Show Custom Dialog [ Get ( ScriptResult ) ]');
INSERT INTO "step_examples" ("id", "script_step_id", "locale", "position", "title", "description", "body") VALUES (430, 22, 'en', 0, 'Example 1', 'Reverts the records in a transaction.', 'Open Transaction []
